From: Project Luma <devnull@projectluma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] menus: native trailing state and individual accelerator keycaps

GTK owns ordinary app and text-edit menu rows. Preserve GtkModelButton action,
shortcut activation and accessible radio/check roles while placing the visible
state at the logical trailing edge. Split parsed modifiers and the key rather
than splitting translated display text on '+', which is itself a valid key.

Based on GTK 4.22.4, LGPL-2.1-or-later. The earlier Luma convergence indicator
fix was inspected against this exact source; no obsolete menu runtime or
quick-action restructuring is restored here.

